From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 16:15:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 44/47] fix(gastown): give polecat agent-home worktrees a
 teardown owner (gcp-actg)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A polecat has two kinds of worktree. The per-bead one at
<home>/worktrees/<bead-id> is found through its bead, and
polecat-worktree-reap.sh reaps it once that bead closes. The persistent
agent HOME at <city>/.gc/worktrees/<rig>/polecats/<agent> has no bead at
all — so every guard the rig owns, all of them bead-keyed, is
structurally blind to it: the reaper excludes homes by construction (its
gate 1 requires a `worktrees/` parent segment), and recover-orphaned-beads
and the work_dir scan both key on a bead whose metadata.work_dir leads to
the worktree. Only a roster-vs-disk diff can see a home, and no step
prescribed one. Reported by the gascity witness as gascity-o963 and
verified by the mayor before filing; the same blindness had already
produced gascity-vst on the nux home.

Nothing was at risk in either instance, but home paths are deterministic
per namepool slot: respawn the slot and the new polecat inherits somebody
else's abandoned checkout, and a non-empty `git status --porcelain` is
exactly what fails submit-and-exit's clean-state check.

This adds assets/scripts/polecat-home-audit.sh, a sweep that issues ZERO
`gc bd` calls — candidates come from `git worktree list`, ownership from
`gc session list` — and wires it as the new `audit-polecat-homes` step in
mol-witness-patrol. Bead keying is the shared root of this whole family
(gascity-18kz, gcp-4k6o), so a bead lookup here would rebuild the bug;
test_gastown_pack_assets.sh now asserts the script contains none.

Four gates, all of which must hold before a home is removed: the path is
`.../polecats/<agent>`; no live session matches the home (on its own
work_dir, or on `<rig>/<agent>` derived from the path); the home hosts no
per-bead child worktrees; and the checkout is clean with nothing
unpublished. The child gate is THE TRAP the bead warns about — when this
was filed, gascity/gastown.rictus was alive and working inside the DEAD
gascity/gastown.furiosa home's subtree, so a naive "home + no session ->
remove" sweep deletes a live polecat's working tree. Any child at all
defers the home, because resolving a child's owner means reading its
bead. Unlike the per-bead reaper this DOES gate on unpublished commits:
that reaper can skip the check because a closed bead is the refinery's
own proof the work landed, and a home has no bead to close — the furiosa
home sat on a detached HEAD holding two commits that belonged to no
branch, and establishing they were superseded took reading content at
origin, which a sweep must not attempt. Those are reported, never
removed. An unreadable session roster ends the run with nothing removed:
reading a failed confirmation as an empty roster is how a sweep concludes
nobody owns anything and clears every home on the rig.

It is a patrol step and NOT a pre_start, deliberately. pre_start is
bounded by [session] setup_timeout and SIGKILLed on overrun, which fails
the whole session start and latches the supervisor circuit breaker after
six failures (gcp-ntbf on the witness, gcp-oo0v on the deacon); the
witness already spends most of that budget on the reaper. It resolves
itself from the formula's own source path, the way mol-deacon-patrol's
detector does. Real removal stays opt-in behind --no-dry-run, matching
the per-bead reaper and the city's posture for the native gascity reaper,
and the patrol invocation does not pass it.

Validation: gastown/tests/test_polecat_home_audit.sh, 11 cases covering
the trap, both ownership keys, the unpublished/detached-HEAD report, the
zero-bead-reads assertion, roster fail-closed, budget truncation, and the
ran-vs-never-ran distinction in the log. All gastown shell tests pass,
plus a dry run against the live gascity-packs rig: 4 homes, correctly
skipping the live occupant and two dirty ones.

Follow-up: two pre-existing test failures on this tree
(tests/test_no_bare_bd_commands.py and gascity test_formula_assets.py)
reproduce unchanged at the fork point ef98960 and are untouched here.
